# Isar Database Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines apply to the design and usage of Isar Database in the project, aimed at optimizing performance, ensuring scalability, and providing the best offline-first experience for users.

## Best Practices
- Define collections with clear and consistent schemas
- Use indexes to optimize frequently used queries
- Implement transactions for complex read-write operations
- Use migrations to safely manage schema changes
- Avoid deep object nesting in schemas to reduce complexity
- Design schemas optimized for querying rather than data normalization
- Use meaningful IDs instead of relying on auto-increment
- Leverage advanced features: full-text search, spatial indexes
- Design data access layer separate from business logic
- Use correct data types to optimize storage and queries

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- Organize Isar-related directory structure:
  ```
  lib/
    ├── data/
    │   ├── datasources/
    │   │   ├── local/
    │   │   │   ├── isar_service.dart           # Initialize Isar and manage connections
    │   │   │   ├── daos/                       # Data Access Objects
    │   │   │   │   ├── message_dao.dart        
    │   │   │   │   └── user_dao.dart
    │   │   │   └── mappers/                    # Mappers between models and entities
    │   │   │       └── message_mapper.dart
    │   ├── models/
    │   │   ├── local/                          # Isar collection models
    │   │   │   ├── message_model.dart
    │   │   │   └── user_model.dart
    └── core/
        ├── database/
            ├── isar_config.dart                # Isar configuration
            ├── migrations/                     # Migrations
            └── constants/                      # Schema versions & constants
  ```

- Collection model template:
  ```dart
  @collection
  class MessageModel {
    Id id = Isar.autoIncrement;
    
    @Index(type: IndexType.value)
    late String remoteId;
    
    @Index(type: IndexType.value)
    late String chatId;
    
    late String content;
    
    @Index(type: IndexType.value)
    late DateTime timestamp;
    
    @Index(type: IndexType.value)
    late MessageStatus status;
    
    // Define enum converter
    @enumerated
    late MessageType type;
  }

  // Type converter extension
  extension MessageStatusConverter on MessageStatus {
    int toIsarValue() => index;
    static MessageStatus fromIsarValue(int value) => MessageStatus.values[value];
  }
  ```

## Initialization & Configuration
- Initializing Isar in the app:
  ```dart
  Future<Isar> initializeDatabase() async {
    final dir = await getApplicationDocumentsDirectory();
    
    // Register schemas
    return Isar.open(
      [MessageModelSchema, UserModelSchema],
      directory: dir.path,
      inspector: kDebugMode, // Enable Isar Inspector in debug mode
    );
  }
  ```

- Dependency injection:
  ```dart
  void setupDatabase(GetIt getIt) {
    // Register Isar instance
    getIt.registerSingletonAsync<Isar>(() => initializeDatabase());
    
    // Register DAOs
    getIt.registerSingletonWithDependencies<MessageDao>(
      () => MessageDao(getIt<Isar>()),
      dependsOn: [Isar],
    );
  }
  ```

## Query & Transaction Patterns
- Data Access Object pattern:
  ```dart
  class MessageDao {
    final Isar _isar;
    
    MessageDao(this._isar);
    
    // Create
    Future<int> saveMessage(MessageModel message) async {
      return _isar.writeTxn(() => _isar.messageModels.put(message));
    }
    
    // Read with streaming for reactive UI
    Stream<List<MessageModel>> watchMessages(String chatId) {
      return _isar.messageModels
          .filter()
          .chatIdEqualTo(chatId)
          .sortByTimestampDesc()
          .watch(fireImmediately: true);
    }
    
    // Update
    Future<void> updateMessageStatus(String remoteId, MessageStatus status) async {
      await _isar.writeTxn(() async {
        final message = await _isar.messageModels
            .filter()
            .remoteIdEqualTo(remoteId)
            .findFirst();
            
        if (message != null) {
          message.status = status;
          await _isar.messageModels.put(message);
        }
      });
    }
    
    // Delete
    Future<void> deleteMessage(String remoteId) async {
      await _isar.writeTxn(() async {
        final message = await _isar.messageModels
            .filter()
            .remoteIdEqualTo(remoteId)
            .findFirst();
            
        if (message != null) {
          await _isar.messageModels.delete(message.id);
        }
      });
    }
    
    // Complex query
    Future<List<MessageModel>> searchMessages(String query) async {
      return _isar.messageModels
          .filter()
          .contentContains(query, caseSensitive: false)
          .sortByTimestampDesc()
          .limit(50)
          .findAll();
    }
  }
  ```

## Migration Strategy
- Managing schema versions and migrations:
  ```dart
  const int kCurrentSchemaVersion = 2;

  Future<void> migrateIfNeeded(Isar isar) async {
    final currentVersion = await getCurrentVersion(isar);
    
    if (currentVersion < kCurrentSchemaVersion) {
      await isar.writeTxn(() async {
        // Apply migrations sequentially
        if (currentVersion < 1) {
          await migrateV1ToV2(isar);
        }
        
        // Update version
        await saveCurrentVersion(isar, kCurrentSchemaVersion);
      });
    }
  }
  ```

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Using appropriate indexes:
  ```dart
  // Composite index for frequent queries
  @collection
  class MessageModel {
    // ...
    
    @Index(composite: [CompositeIndex('timestamp')])
    late String chatId;
    
    late DateTime timestamp;
  }
  ```

- Avoiding N+1 queries with links & backlinks:
  ```dart
  @collection
  class ChatModel {
    Id id = Isar.autoIncrement;
    
    late String title;
    
    // Define links to related collections
    final participants = IsarLinks<UserModel>();
    final messages = IsarLinks<MessageModel>();
  }
  
  // Using links in queries
  Future<ChatModel> getChatWithMessages(String chatId) async {
    final chat = await isar.chatModels
        .filter()
        .remoteIdEqualTo(chatId)
        .findFirst();
        
    // Load related collections in one go
    await chat?.messages.load();
    await chat?.participants.load();
    
    return chat!;
  }
  ```

- Reading batch data for performance optimization:
  ```dart
  Future<List<MessageModel>> getMessagesByIds(List<String> remoteIds) async {
    return isar.messageModels
        .filter()
        .anyOf(
          remoteIds,
          (q, id) => q.remoteIdEqualTo(id),
        )
        .findAll();
  }
  ```

## Sync Strategies
- Creating sync change tracker:
  ```dart
  @collection
  class SyncQueueItem {
    Id id = Isar.autoIncrement;
    
    late String entityId;
    late String entityType;
    late SyncAction action;
    late DateTime createdAt;
    
    @enumerated
    late SyncStatus status;
  }
  
  enum SyncAction { create, update, delete }
  enum SyncStatus { pending, inProgress, completed, failed }
  ```

- Service for syncing from local to server:
  ```dart
  Future<void> synchronizeChanges() async {
    final pendingItems = await _isar.syncQueueItems
        .filter()
        .statusEqualTo(SyncStatus.pending)
        .sortByCreatedAt()
        .findAll();
        
    for (final item in pendingItems) {
      try {
        await _isar.writeTxn(() async {
          item.status = SyncStatus.inProgress;
          await _isar.syncQueueItems.put(item);
        });
        
        bool success = false;
        switch (item.entityType) {
          case 'message':
            success = await _syncMessage(item);
            break;
          // Other entity types...
        }
        
        await _isar.writeTxn(() async {
          item.status = success ? SyncStatus.completed : SyncStatus.failed;
          await _isar.syncQueueItems.put(item);
        });
      } catch (e) {
        await _isar.writeTxn(() async {
          item.status = SyncStatus.failed;
          await _isar.syncQueueItems.put(item);
        });
      }
    }
  }
  ```

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Creating a separate test database instance:
  ```dart
  Future<Isar> getTestDatabase() async {
    final dir = await Directory.systemTemp.createTemp('isar_test');
    return Isar.open(
      [MessageModelSchema, UserModelSchema],
      directory: dir.path,
    );
  }
  ```

- Unit testing DAOs:
  ```dart
  void main() {
    late Isar isar;
    late MessageDao messageDao;
    
    setUp(() async {
      isar = await getTestDatabase();
      messageDao = MessageDao(isar);
    });
    
    tearDown(() async {
      await isar.close(deleteFromDisk: true);
    });
    
    test('should save and retrieve message', () async {
      // Arrange
      final message = MessageModel()
        ..remoteId = 'msg1'
        ..chatId = 'chat1'
        ..content = 'Hello'
        ..timestamp = DateTime.now()
        ..status = MessageStatus.sent
        ..type = MessageType.text;
        
      // Act
      final id = await messageDao.saveMessage(message);
      final result = await messageDao.getMessageByRemoteId('msg1');
      
      // Assert
      expect(result, isNotNull);
      expect(result!.content, equals('Hello'));
    });
  }
  ```

## Error Handling Strategies
- Database error handling:
  ```dart
  Future<Result<List<MessageModel>>> getMessages(String chatId) async {
    try {
      final messages = await _isar.messageModels
          .filter()
          .chatIdEqualTo(chatId)
          .sortByTimestampDesc()
          .findAll();
          
      return Result.success(messages);
    } catch (e, stackTrace) {
      _logger.error('Error fetching messages', e, stackTrace);
      return Result.failure(DatabaseFailure('Failed to fetch messages'));
    }
  }
  ```

- Building repository layer using failure types:
  ```dart
  @injectable
  class MessageRepositoryImpl implements MessageRepository {
    final MessageDao _messageDao;
    final MessageMapper _mapper;
    
    MessageRepositoryImpl(this._messageDao, this._mapper);
    
    @override
    Future<Either<Failure, List<Message>>> getMessages(String chatId) async {
      try {
        final result = await _messageDao.getMessages(chatId);
        return result.when(
          success: (models) => Right(models.map(_mapper.toDomain).toList()),
          failure: (error) => Left(error),
        );
      } catch (e) {
        return Left(CacheFailure(e.toString()));
      }
    }
  }
  ```
